# NO SECRETS HERE. Token lives in ~/.config/tts-bot/token (chmod 600), see README.
# First-boot SEED only: used once to populate config.json when it does not exist yet.
# After that the web UI / config.json is the source of truth and this value is ignored.
# Right-click the text channel in Discord (Developer Mode on) -> Copy Channel ID
TTS_CHANNEL_ID=
COMMAND_PREFIX=!
PIPER_MODEL_PATH=models/en_US-lessac-medium.onnx
PIPER_CONFIG_PATH=models/en_US-lessac-medium.onnx.json
MAX_CHARS=300
MAX_QUEUE=20
STATE_FILE=state.json
# Optional override of token file location
# DISCORD_TOKEN_FILE=~/.config/tts-bot/token
# Runtime config (channel selection) written by the web UI
# CONFIG_FILE=state/config.json   (default: next to STATE_FILE)
# Web UI: binds loopback by default; access via SSH tunnel
# WEBUI_HOST=127.0.0.1
# WEBUI_PORT=8765
# GUI token file (>= 24 chars, else the GUI is disabled); generate with scripts/gen_gui_token.sh
# WEBUI_TOKEN_FILE=/home/you/.config/tts-bot/gui_token   (no ~ expansion)
